      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "Adult dose (IV)",
          "text": "• Dose by weight and levels, not a fixed dose: usual maintenance 15 to 20 mg/kg (actual body weight) every 8 to 12 hours, adjusted to renal function and levels.\n• Loading dose in critically ill patients or with serious infection: 20 to 35 mg/kg actual body weight, usually capped at 3 g.\n• Infuse no faster than 1 g an hour (10 mg/min), and slower for larger doses, to reduce infusion reactions.\n• Target an AUC/MIC of 400 to 600 (assuming an MIC of 1 mg/L) over 24 hours, per the 2020 ASHP/IDSA consensus guideline.\n• See the TDM tab for monitoring approaches."
