          "text": "• Oral vancomycin is not absorbed, so it works only inside the gut.\n• Initial non-severe or severe episode: 125 mg four times a day for 10 days (fidaxomicin is preferred if available).\n• Fulminant infection: 500 mg four times a day by mouth or nasogastric tube, plus IV metronidazole, with rectal vancomycin if ileus is present.\n• Recurrence: a tapered and pulsed regimen is one option; seek specialist advice."
        },
        {
          "title": "Renal adjustment",
          "text": "• Dose by levels in all patients with renal impairment.\n• Start with a loading dose, then use a nomogram or pharmacokinetic software to set the interval: for example, every 24 hours at CrCl 30 to 50, and dosing by level when CrCl is below 30 or unstable.\n• Haemodialysis: dose after each session, guided by pre-dialysis levels.\n• Do not adjust oral vancomycin for renal function."
