          "text": "• Extended-interval (once-daily): 5 to 7 mg/kg IV every 24 hours; many hospitals use 5 mg/kg for pyelonephritis and urosepsis, and 7 mg/kg with a nomogram for severe sepsis.\n• Traditional (multiple daily): 1.5 to 2 mg/kg IV loading dose, then 1 to 1.7 mg/kg every 8 hours.\n• Synergy in endocarditis (with a beta-lactam or vancomycin): 1 mg/kg every 8 hours for staphylococci and enterococci; for viridans streptococci, 3 mg/kg a day in one or three divided doses, per AHA guidance.\n• Use ideal body weight, or adjusted body weight in obesity: IBW + 0.4 x (actual weight minus IBW).\n• Infuse over 30 to 60 minutes; give gentamicin separately from beta-lactams, which can inactivate it in the same bag."
