          "title": "Adult dose",
          "text": "• Community-acquired pneumonia and atypical cover: 500 mg orally or IV once a day, usually 3 to 5 days.\n• Five-day course: 500 mg on day 1, then 250 mg daily for days 2 to 5.\n• Chlamydia (alternative to doxycycline, for example in pregnancy): 1 g orally as a single dose.\n• Pertussis: 500 mg on day 1, then 250 mg daily for 4 days.\n• Cholera: 1 g orally as a single dose; travellers' diarrhoea: 1 g single dose, or 500 mg daily for up to 3 days.\n• MAC prophylaxis in advanced HIV, when ART is not started immediately and CD4 is below 50: 1200 mg once a week; MAC treatment: 250 to 500 mg daily, always with other drugs.\n• Trachoma mass treatment: 20 mg/kg single dose; azithromycin is no longer recommended as dual therapy for gonorrhoea in current CDC guidance."
