          "text": "• Standard: 100 mg orally or IV every 12 hours (a 200 mg loading dose on day 1 is used in some regimens).\n• Community-acquired pneumonia and atypical cover: 100 mg every 12 hours for 5 to 7 days.\n• Rocky Mountain spotted fever and other rickettsial disease: 100 mg every 12 hours; start on suspicion and continue until afebrile for at least 3 days.\n• Early Lyme disease with erythema migrans: 100 mg every 12 hours for 10 days; Lyme prophylaxis after a high-risk tick bite: 200 mg once, within 72 hours.\n• Chlamydia and non-gonococcal urethritis: 100 mg every 12 hours for 7 days; syphilis in penicillin allergy: 100 mg every 12 hours for 14 days (early) or 28 days (late).\n• Malaria prophylaxis: 100 mg once a day, starting 1 to 2 days before travel and continuing 4 weeks after leaving; anthrax post-exposure and treatment: 100 mg every 12 hours.\n• Doxycycline post-exposure prophylaxis for bacterial STIs (selected high-risk groups): 200 mg once within 72 hours after sex, per CDC guidance."
