          "title": "Spectrum and uses",
          "text": "• Active against Enterobacterales, Pseudomonas aeruginosa, Haemophilus, Neisseria, Campylobacter, Salmonella, Shigella, Bacillus anthracis and Yersinia pestis.\n• Common uses: complicated urinary infection and pyelonephritis (where resistance is low), traveller's and bacterial diarrhoea, bone and joint infection (Gram-negative), prostatitis, and post-exposure prophylaxis.\n• Poor activity against streptococci and pneumococci, anaerobes, and MRSA; resistance among E. coli, Pseudomonas and Neisseria gonorrhoeae is widespread."
