          "text": "• Boxed warning: tendinitis and tendon rupture, peripheral neuropathy, central nervous system effects, and worsening of myasthenia gravis; avoid for mild infections when other options exist.\n• Risk of tendon injury rises with age over 60, corticosteroids, kidney, heart or lung transplant.\n• Aortic aneurysm and dissection: avoid in patients with known aneurysm or at high risk.\n• Dysglycaemia (especially with diabetes drugs), QT prolongation, photosensitivity, and C. difficile infection.\n• Interactions: chelation with antacids, iron, zinc, calcium and sucralfate (take ciprofloxacin 2 hours before or 6 hours after); contraindicated with tizanidine; raises theophylline and caffeine levels; increases warfarin effect."
