          "text": "• Standard double-strength (DS) tablet: 160 mg trimethoprim with 800 mg sulfamethoxazole.\n• Uncomplicated cystitis: 1 DS tablet every 12 hours for 3 days.\n• Skin and soft tissue infection (MRSA): 1 to 2 DS tablets every 12 hours.\n• Pneumocystis pneumonia treatment: trimethoprim 15 to 20 mg/kg a day (IV or oral) in 3 to 4 divided doses for 21 days; mild to moderate disease can use oral dosing, such as 2 DS tablets every 8 hours.\n• Pneumocystis prophylaxis: 1 DS or 1 single-strength tablet daily, or 1 DS three times a week.\n• Stenotrophomonas maltophilia: 8 to 12 mg/kg a day (trimethoprim component) IV in 2 to 3 divided doses, usually combined with another agent per IDSA AMR guidance.\n• Nocardia: 10 to 15 mg/kg a day (trimethoprim component) in divided doses, adjusted by specialist advice."
