          "text": "• CrCl above 30 mL/min: no change.\n• CrCl 15 to 30: give 50% of the usual dose.\n• CrCl below 15: avoid, or give 50% of the usual dose with close monitoring; for Pneumocystis, specialist advice is needed.\n• Haemodialysis: dose after the session.\n• Trimethoprim blocks tubular secretion of creatinine, so serum creatinine can rise by up to 0.3 to 0.4 mg/dL without a true drop in GFR."
