          "text": "• Active against many Enterobacterales (resistance is common), MRSA and MSSA, Stenotrophomonas maltophilia, Nocardia, Pneumocystis jirovecii, Toxoplasma, Listeria and Burkholderia pseudomallei.\n• Common uses: urinary infection (where local resistance is below about 20%), community MRSA skin infection, Pneumocystis treatment and prophylaxis, Stenotrophomonas, nocardiosis, melioidosis eradication phase, and Listeria in penicillin allergy.\n• Not reliable for streptococcal pharyngitis, enterococci in vivo, or anaerobes."
