          "text": "• Anaerobic and mixed infection: 500 mg IV or orally every 8 hours (some guidelines use 500 mg every 12 hours for convenience).\n• Bacterial vaginosis: 500 mg orally every 12 hours for 7 days; trichomoniasis in women: 500 mg every 12 hours for 7 days; in men: 2 g orally as a single dose (CDC).\n• Amoebic colitis and liver abscess: 500 to 750 mg orally three times a day for 7 to 10 days, followed by a luminal agent such as paromomycin.\n• Giardiasis: 250 mg three times a day for 5 to 7 days (or 2 g once a day for 3 days in some guidelines).\n• C. difficile: no longer first-line; use only if fidaxomicin and vancomycin are unavailable, for non-severe disease, and as an IV adjunct in fulminant infection.\n• Oral and IV doses are equivalent."
