          "title": "Cautions and monitoring",
          "text": "• Neurotoxicity and seizures if the dose is not reduced for renal impairment.\n• Hypersensitivity: cross-reactivity with other cephalosporins is possible, and it shares the ceftazidime side chain with aztreonam.\n• Diarrhoea, C. difficile infection and a positive Coombs test are possible.\n• Keep it for infections where it is needed, because resistance to it has emerged, including through KPC variants."
